s://github.com/bsach64/bhshell.git`\\\n`cd bhshell`\\\n`make bhshell`\\\nIf you want to run tests\\\n    `make test`\\\n`./bhshell`\n\n## TODO\n- [x] Understand how creating processes actually works\n- [x] Simulate the \"|\" operator\n- [x] Rewrite for better organisation and error handling\n    - [x] Rewrite to use xmalloc\n    - [x] Add tests\n- [x] prompt shows current working directory\n- [x] Remove `exit(EXIT_FAILURE)`\n- [x] Rewrite the Parser {Basically}\n    - [x] Simulate the \">\" operator of $BASH\n    - [x] Allow for the \"|\" operator of $BASH\n- [ ] Maybe\n    - [ ] Support multiple \">\" {allowing for `ls > file1.txt > file2.txt`}\n    - [ ] Escape characters etc {echo \"wow\" should print wow instead of \"wow\"}\n    - [ ] Implement some level of globbing (Meaning *.txt means all .txt files in the current dir)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d509166a-366a-46f7-9e64-b6bd767e6174","uuid":"b810872a-11cb-4de3-a433-3fbb3b2d33ea","timestamp":"2026-05-29T14:30:53.015Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"c_src/src:\ntotal 36\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 scheschb amazon 4096 May 29 14:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 scheschb amazon 4096 May 29 14:30 ..\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 5165 May 29 14:30 bhshell.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  835 May 29 14:30 dynamicarr.c\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 scheschb amazon 4096 May 29 14:30 include\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 2724 May 29 14:30 input.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  197 May 29 14:30 main.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  400 May 29 14:30 xalloc.c\n\nc_src/tests:\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 scheschb amazon 4096 May 29 14:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 scheschb amazon 4096 May 29 14:30 ..\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 2998 May 29 14:30 test.c\n\nsrc/interfaces:\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 scheschb amazon 4096 May 29 14:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 scheschb amazon 4096 May 29 14:30 ..\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  129 May 29 14:30 main.rs\nCC = gcc\nCFLAGS = -Wall -Wextra -Wno-unused-variable -Wno-unused-parameter -fprofile-arcs -ftest-coverage -fPIC\nL